    background:var(--sky-500);color:#fff;font-size:1.2rem;
    box-shadow:0 4px 14px rgba(14,165,233,.35);
    opacity:0;pointer-events:none;transition:opacity .3s,transform .3s;
    transform:translateY(10px);
  }
  #scrollTop.visible{opacity:1;pointer-events:auto;transform:translateY(0)}
  #scrollTop:hover{background:var(--sky-600)}

  /* ── Footer ── */
  .footer{text-align:center;padding:2rem 1rem;color:var(--sky-700);font-size:.82rem;opacity:.65}

  /* ── Responsive ── */
  @media(max-width:768px){
    .col-headers,.section-row{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .hero h1{font-size:1.8rem}
    .hero .zh{font-size:1.3rem}
    .container{padding:1rem}
    nav .brand{font-size:.95rem}
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ── Sticky Nav ── -->
<nav>
  <span class="brand">🌤️ Sky</span>
  <div class="nav-links">
    <a href="#toddler">Toddler / 小朋友</a>
    <a href="#teens">Teen / 高中生</a>
    <a href="#phd">PhD / 博士</a>
  </div>
</nav>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ── Hero ── -->
  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue?</h1>
    <div class="zh">为什么天空是蓝色的？</div>
    <div class="bar"></div>
  </header>

  <!-- ── Column headers ── -->
  <div class="col-headers">
    <div class="col-header">🇬🇧 English</div>
    <div class="col-header">🇨🇳 中文（简体）</div>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════ SECTION 1: TODDLER ═══════════ -->
  <div class="section-row" id="toddler">
    <div class="card">
      <h2><span class="badge badge-toddler">Toddler · Age 3</span> For a 3-Year-Old Toddler</h2>
      <p>Imagine sunlight is like a bunch of tiny colored balls — red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple — all flying through the air together. When those little balls hit the tiny, tiny air particles (like invisible bubbles) in the sky, the blue ones bounce around the most, everywhere you can see. That's why the sky looks blue! It's like blue is the color that gets to dance around the most when the sun's light hits the air.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2><span class="badge badge-toddler">小朋友 · 3岁</span> 给3岁小朋友</h2>
      <p>想象一下，阳光就像一大堆彩色的小球——红的、橙的、黄的、绿的、蓝的、紫的——它们一起在空气中飞行。当这些小球碰到天空里那些超级小的空气粒子（就像看不见的小泡泡）时，蓝色的小球弹得最厉害，到处都是。所以天空看起来是蓝色的！就像是阳光碰到空气时，蓝色是跳得最欢的颜色。</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════ SECTION 2: HIGH SCHOOL ═══════════ -->
  <div class="section-row" id="teens">
    <div class="card">
      <h2><span class="badge badge-teens">High School</span> For a High School Teenager</h2>
      <p>The sky is blue due to <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>. Here's the short version:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Sunlight (white light) is actually a mix of all visible wavelengths (colors).</li>
        <li>As sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it interacts with gas molecules (mostly N<sub>2</sub> and O<sub>2</sub>).</li>
        <li>Shorter wavelengths (blue, ~450 nm) scatter much more strongly than longer wavelengths (red, ~700 nm). The scattering intensity is proportional to 1/<span class="m">λ</span><span class="mup">4</span> (inverse fourth power of wavelength).</li>
        <li>This means blue light is scattered in all directions ~5.5× more than red light, which is why the sky appears blue when you look away from the sun.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Why not violet then?</strong> Violet light (~400 nm) scatters even more than blue. But:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>The Sun emits less violet light than blue light.</li>
        <li>Our eyes are less sensitive to violet.</li>
        <li>Some violet is absorbed in the upper atmosphere.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The net effect is that blue dominates the perceived color.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2><span class="badge badge-teens">高中生</span> 给高中生</h2>
      <p>天空是蓝色的，这是由<strong>瑞利散射</strong>造成的。简单来说：</p>
      <ul>
        <li>阳光（白光）实际上包含了所有可见光波长（颜色）的混合。</li>
        <li>当阳光进入地球大气层时，它会与气体分子（主要是 N<sub>2</sub> 和 O<sub>2</sub>）发生相互作用。</li>
        <li>较短的波长（蓝色，约 450 nm）比波长较长的光（红色，约 700 nm）散射得更强烈。散射强度与 1/<span class="m">λ</span><span class="mup">4</span> 成正比（波长的四次方倒数）。</li>
        <li>这意味着蓝光在各个方向上的散射比红光强大约 5.5 倍，这就是为什么当你不看太阳时，天空呈现蓝色。</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>那为什么不是紫色呢？</strong> 紫光（约 400 nm）的散射甚至比蓝光还强。但是：</p>
      <ol>
        <li>太阳发出的紫光比蓝光少。</li>
        <li>我们的眼睛对紫光不太敏感。</li>
        <li>部分紫光被高层大气吸收了。</li>
      </ol>
      <p>综合效果就是蓝色主导了我们看到的天空颜色。</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════ SECTION 3: PHYSICS PHD ═══════════ -->
  <div class="section-row" id="phd">
    <!-- ── English PhD ── -->
    <div class="card">
      <h2><span class="badge badge-phd">Physics PhD</span> For a Physics PhD</h2>

      <p>The phenomenon is governed by <strong>elastic scattering of electromagnetic radiation by particles much smaller than the incident wavelength</strong> — in this case, air molecules with a characteristic size of ~3 Å, compared to visible wavelengths of 400–700 nm.</p>

      <h3>Microscopic mechanism</h3>
      <p>A single air molecule, in the non-resonant (far-off-resonance) limit, acts as a polarizable dielectric. The incident electric field <span class="mb">E</span> induces a dipole moment:</p>

      <div class="formula">
        <span class="eq"><span class="mb">p</span> = α<span class="mb">E</span></span>
      </div>

      <p>where <span class="m">α</span> is the polarizability tensor. The re-radiated (scattered) field falls off as a dipole radiation pattern with a characteristic <span class="m">1/r</span> dependence in the far field. The differential cross-section for a single molecule is:</p>

      <div class="formula">
        <span class="eq">
          <span class="m">dσ/dΩ</span> =
          <span class="fr"><span class="n"><span class="m">k</span><sub>0</sub><span class="mup">4</span> <span class="m">α</span><span class="mup">2</span></span><span class="d">16<span class="m">π</span><span class="mup">2</span> <span class="m">ε</span><sub>0</sub><span class="mup">2</span></span></span>
          &thinsp;·&thinsp;
          <span class="fr"><span class="n">(1 − |<span class="m">k̂</span> · <span class="m">k̂</span>′|)<span class="mup">2</span></span><span class="d">2</span></span>
        </span>
      </div>

      <p>where <span class="m">k</span><sub>0</sub> = 2<span class="m">π</span>/<span class="m">λ</span> is the wave number, and the angular dependence gives the characteristic dipole pattern (zero scattering along the propagation direction, maximum at 90°).</p>

      <h3>The 1/λ⁴ dependence</h3>
      <p>Integrating over solid angle yields the Rayleigh scattering cross-section:</p>

      <div class="formula">
        <span class="eq">
          <span class="m">σ</span><sub>R</sub> =
          <span class="fr"><span class="n">8<span class="m">π</span></span><span class="d">3</span></span>
          &thinsp;
          <span class="m">k</span><sub>0</sub><span class="mup">4</span>
          &thinsp;
          <span class="fr"><span class="n"><span class="m">α</span></span><span class="d">4<span class="m">π</span><span class="m">ε</span><sub>0</sub></span></span><span class="mup">2</span>
        </span>
      </div>

      <p>The key point: <span class="key-result"><span class="m">σ</span><sub>R</sub> ∝ <span class="m">λ</span><sup>−4</sup></span>. This arises because the induced dipole moment scales as <span class="m">ω</span><span class="mup">2</span><span class="m">α</span> (from the equation of motion of a bound oscillator in the far-off-resonance limit), and the scattered intensity scales as the fourth power of frequency.</p>

      <h3>Why the sky is blue and not violet (quantitatively)</h3>
      <p>The full sky color is the convolution of:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Solar spectrum</strong> <span class="m">S</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) — peaks in the visible, with lower flux in the violet than blue.</li>
        <li><strong>Rayleigh optical depth</strong> <span class="m">τ</span><sub>R</sub>(<span class="m">λ</span>) = <span class="m">N</span><span class="m">σ</span><sub>R</sub>(<span class="m">λ</span>), where <span class="m">N</span> is the column density of air molecules.</li>
        <li><strong>Atmospheric transmittance</strong> <span class="m">T</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) = <span class="m">e</span><sup>−<span class="m">τ</span><sub>tot</sub></sup> (including aerosol/Mie scattering and absorption).</li>
        <li><strong>Human photopic response</strong> <span class="m">V</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) — the CIE 1931 luminosity function, weighted for the blue cone (S-cone) contribution.</li>
      </ol>

      <p>The perceived color of the clear sky is dominated by the <span class="m">τ</span><sub>R</sub> ≪ 1 (single-scattering) regime near the zenith, where the spectral radiance is proportional to <span class="m">S</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) · <span class="m">σ</span><sub>R</sub>(<span class="m">λ</span>) · sin<span class="m">θ</span> d<span class="m">Ω</span>. The product of the decreasing violet output of the sun, the rising <span class="m">λ</span><sup>−4</sup> scattering, and the eye's lower S-cone sensitivity produces the perceived blue.</p>

      <h3>Beyond Rayleigh: Mie and depolarization</h3>
      <p>For aerosol particles with size parameter <span class="m">x</span> = 2<span class="m">πr</span>/<span class="m">λ</span> ≳ 1, Mie scattering applies. The angular dependence is strongly forward-peaked (the "Mie lobe"), and the color dependence is much weaker (<span class="m">≈ λ</span><sup>−<span class="m">α</span></sup> with <span class="m">α</span> ≈ 0.5–2 depending on the size distribution). This is why:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Hazy skies appear white/washed-out (multiple scattering + Mie forward lobe).</li>
        <li>Sunset/sunrise colors are red/orange: at low solar elevation, the slant optical path length <span class="m">L</span> ≈ 1/cos<span class="m">θ</span><sub>zenith</sub> is large enough that blue light is essentially fully Rayleigh-scattered out of the direct beam before reaching the observer, while red light (weakly scattered) survives.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>The polarization of scattered skylight (elliptically polarized, with maximum linear polarization at the <strong>Brewster angle</strong> <span class="m">θ</span><sub>B</sub> ≈ 53.5° from the solar direction for <span class="m">n</span> ≈ 1.0003) provides a direct experimental confirmation of the transverse-wave nature of light and the dipole scattering geometry.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Chinese PhD ── -->
    <div class="card">
      <h2><span class="badge badge-phd">物理学博士</span> 给物理学博士</h2>

      <p>这一现象由<strong>电磁辐射被远小于入射波长的粒子的弹性散射</strong>所主导——具体而言，是特征尺寸约 3 Å 的空气分子对 400–700 nm 可见光波长的散射。</p>

      <h3>微观机制</h3>
      <p>单个空气分子在远离共振（非共振）极限下表现为可极化介质。入射电场 <span class="mb">E</span> 感应出电偶极矩：</p>

      <div class="formula">
        <span class="eq"><span class="mb">p</span> = α<span class="mb">E</span></span>
      </div>

      <p>其中 <span class="m">α</span> 为极化率张量。再辐射（散射）场按偶极辐射图案衰减，在远场中具有特征性的 <span class="m">1/r</span> 依赖关系。单个分子微分散射截面为：</p>

      <div class="formula">
        <span class="eq">
          <span class="m">dσ/dΩ</span> =
          <span class="fr"><span class="n"><span class="m">k</span><sub>0</sub><span class="mup">4</span> <span class="m">α</span><span class="mup">2</span></span><span class="d">16<span class="m">π</span><span class="mup">2</span> <span class="m">ε</span><sub>0</sub><span class="mup">2</span></span></span>
          &thinsp;·&thinsp;
          <span class="fr"><span class="n">(1 − |<span class="m">k̂</span> · <span class="m">k̂</span>′|)<span class="mup">2</span></span><span class="d">2</span></span>
        </span>
      </div>

      <p>其中 <span class="m">k</span><sub>0</sub> = 2<span class="m">π</span>/<span class="m">λ</span> 为波数，角度依赖关系给出特征性的偶极图案（沿传播方向散射为零，90° 时最大）。</p>

      <h3>1/λ⁴ 依赖关系</h3>
      <p>对立体角积分可得瑞利散射截面：</p>

      <div class="formula">
        <span class="eq">
          <span class="m">σ</span><sub>R</sub> =
          <span class="fr"><span class="n">8<span class="m">π</span></span><span class="d">3</span></span>
          &thinsp;
          <span class="m">k</span><sub>0</sub><span class="mup">4</span>
          &thinsp;
          <span class="fr"><span class="n"><span class="m">α</span></span><span class="d">4<span class="m">π</span><span class="m">ε</span><sub>0</sub></span></span><span class="mup">2</span>
        </span>
      </div>

      <p>关键点：<span class="key-result"><span class="m">σ</span><sub>R</sub> ∝ <span class="m">λ</span><sup>−4</sup></span>。这是因为感应偶极矩按 <span class="m">ω</span><span class="mup">2</span><span class="m">α</span> 缩放（来源于束缚振子运动方程在远离共振极限下的解），而散射强度按频率的四次方缩放。</p>

      <h3>为什么天空是蓝色而非紫色（定量分析）</h3>
      <p>天空颜色的完整描述是以下因素的卷积：</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>太阳光谱</strong> <span class="m">S</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) — 峰值在可见光区域，紫光通量低于蓝光。</li>
        <li><strong>瑞利光学厚度</strong> <span class="m">τ</span><sub>R</sub>(<span class="m">λ</span>) = <span class="m">N</span><span class="m">σ</span><sub>R</sub>(<span class="m">λ</span>)，其中 <span class="m">N</span> 为空气分子柱密度。</li>
        <li><strong>大气透过率</strong> <span class="m">T</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) = <span class="m">e</span><sup>−<span class="m">τ</span><sub>tot</sub></sup>（包含气溶胶/米氏散射和吸收）。</li>
        <li><strong>人眼明视觉响应</strong> <span class="m">V</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) — CIE 1931 光度函数，加权考虑了蓝色锥细胞（S 型锥体）的贡献。</li>
      </ol>

      <p>晴空的颜色感知主要由天顶附近 <span class="m">τ</span><sub>R</sub> ≪ 1（单次散射）区域主导，该区域的光谱辐射亮度与 <span class="m">S</span>(<span class="m">λ</span>) · <span class="m">σ</span><sub>R</sub>(<span class="m">λ</span>) · sin<span class="m">θ</span> d<span class="m">Ω</span> 成正比。太阳紫光输出的减少、<span class="m">λ</span><sup>−4</sup> 散射的增强以及眼睛 S 型锥细胞较低敏感度的乘积，产生了我们感知到的蓝色。</p>

      <h3>超越瑞利：米氏散射与去偏振</h3>
      <p>对于尺寸参数 <span class="m">x</span> = 2<span class="m">πr</span>/<span class="m">λ</span> ≳ 1 的气溶胶粒子，米氏散射适用。角度依赖关系呈强烈的前向峰值（"米氏瓣"），颜色依赖关系弱得多（<span class="m">≈ λ</span><sup>−<span class="m">α</span></sup>，其中 <span class="m">α</span> ≈ 0.5–2，取决于粒径分布）。这就是为什么：</p>
      <ul>
        <li>有雾霾的天空呈现白色/灰白色（多次散射 + 米氏前向瓣）。</li>
        <li>日出/日落颜色为红色/橙色：在太阳高度角较低时，倾斜光程长度 <span class="m">L</span> ≈ 1/cos<span class="m">θ</span><sub>zenith</sub> 足够大，蓝光在到达观察者之前基本被瑞利散射出直射光，而红光（散射较弱）得以保留。</li>
      </ul>

      <p>散射天空光的偏振（椭圆偏振，在线偏振最大处位于<strong>布儒斯特角</strong> <span class="m">θ</span><sub>B</sub> ≈ 53.5°，相对于太阳方向，折射率 <span class="m">n</span> ≈ 1.0003）直接证实了光的横波性质和偶极散射几何结构。</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Footer ── -->
  <footer class="footer">
    Why Is the Sky Blue? &middot; 为什么天空是蓝色的？
  </footer>
</div>

<!-- ── Scroll to top ── -->
<button id="scrollTop" aria-label="Scroll to top">&#8679;</button>

<script>
  const btn = document.getElementById('scrollTop');
  window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
    btn.classList.toggle('visible', window.scrollY > 400);
  });
  btn.addEventListener('click', () => window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' }));
</script>
</body>
</html>
"}

